Termodinâmica — Bernhard Lesche, UFJF (@th-lesche: 0, is #reference, #part-of @th-sources) { r_0ABCKSRZBN8T4Y4FV1FQPWNY4Z
Bernhard Lesche, Universidade Federal de Juiz de Fora. [Department notes index](https://www2.ufjf.br/fisica/disciplinas/notas-de-aulas/bernhard-johannes-lesche/temodinamica/) · [Introduction, dated 30 April 2014](https://www2.ufjf.br/fisica/files/2019/09/CAP-01-2014-04-30.pdf) · [Second law, dated 10 May 2011](https://www2.ufjf.br/fisica/wp-content/uploads/sites/427/2019/09/CAP-04-2011-05-10.pdf) · [Thermodynamic potentials](https://www2.ufjf.br/fisica/files/2019/09/CAP-05-2014-04-30.pdf).

Read the complete available Portuguese chapter sequence and solve its derivations/exercises as a companion to [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1). The verified introductory chapter develops why macroscopic mechanics needs additional state information; the later linked chapters deepen second-law reasoning and potentials. Compare definitions and work signs explicitly across languages.

The department's sitemap identifies the notes, but the chapter-index retrieval failed on 29 October 2026. The 32-page introductory PDF was accessible and other chapter metadata indexed; complete inspection of every chapter is not claimed. Filenames carry distinct revision dates, not one inferred publication year. Institutional public hosting does not establish a blanket open-adaptation licence. All chapters remain external.

**Return:** [Thermodynamics and heat transfer sources](../Sources.lingua#r_4N96T70VYW3C3M91M2SXF5KEQF).
